    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "**ChatGPT independent review, exact HEAD `8b802f37f3e4b1da3512cc1e26ac4d98e9019496`: CHANGES REQUIRED before merge.** Formal GitHub `REQUEST_CHANGES` was rejected (the authenticated account owns this PR), so this is a blocking review finding in the PR conversation rather than a GitHub review-state change.\n\n**Mobile keyboard / open-menu boundary defect risk:** `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`, `ensureMobilePinnedChatLayout().sync`, allows `minPanelHeight` to shrink to 0 at small `visualViewport` heights or with menu open, yet later unconditionally sets `panelsHeight = Math.max(88, ...)`. Meanwhile `minChatHeight` has a 72px floor even when chat header, composer and splitter need more space. With short visual viewport + open menu, fixed chrome + chat + min panel can exceed visible space; CSS `overflow:hidden` may clip the composer or lower panel. This is a concrete risk from the code arithmetic, **not** claimed Safari reproduction.\n\nThe regression runner currently fakes a reduced `visualViewport` only with the menu closed and verifies class/CSS values; it does **not** test composer/panel visible geometry under a keyboard with menu open. To resolve on the existing #431 branch: add short viewport / menu-open / keyboard regression with actual DOM bounds vs visual viewport, nonzero scrollable chat/feed, focused input reachability, keyboard show/hide restoration. Explicitly handle impossible geometry (e.g. collapse menu while editing) without duplicate mobile handlers. Run browser checks and preserve both Web/docs mirrors. Keep PR Draft; no merge, Chat04.1 PR #453, Chat03, Stage7.15, Cloudflare.\n\nVerified: 5 permitted changed paths, clean mergeable GitHub state, forensics run #40867459087 SUCCESS. That workflow does not execute the mobile DOM runner. Physical Safari acceptance remains separate.",
